+## 10. Cost-telemetry markers **[NORMATIVE]** (added 2026-08-07)
+
+Cost tracking rides the GitHub comment/body markers — **the 5-field ack (§2) is unchanged**
+(Kyber's `worker-acks` binding renders only its declared fields; usage travels where the durable
+record already lives). Three markers, all single-line hidden HTML comments with inline JSON, all
+machine-produced (`scripts/token-usage.sh` for the first two; Lando for the third). If serialized
+JSON ever contains `--`, the producer falls back to a bare marker + fenced ```json block.
+
+### 10.1 `falcon:usage-baseline:v1` — worker, INSIDE the `falcon:pickup` comment
+
+The worker's transcript odometer at stage pickup. Written by `token-usage.sh baseline
+<envelope_id> --marker`. Cached in the identity repo's `.runtime/`; the comment copy is the
+recovery source after a pod recycle.
+
+```json
+{"v":1,"envelope_id":"…","taken_at":"<iso8601>",
+ "files":{"<transcript path>":{"size":123,"models":{"<model>":{"input":0,"output":0,"cache_read":0,"cache_creation":0,"api_calls":0}}}},
+ "totals":{"<model>":{"input":0,"output":0,"cache_read":0,"cache_creation":0,"api_calls":0}}}
+```
+
+### 10.2 `falcon:usage:v1` — worker, INSIDE the `falcon:complete` comment
+
+The stage's usage delta (now − baseline), per ACTUAL model from the transcript (planned models
+live in the mini-charter; Lando flags mismatches). Written by `token-usage.sh report
+<envelope_id> --stage <stage_label> --issue <owner/repo#N> --marker`. Review/deploy stages post
+it on the PR (with their completion comment); Lando's close-path aggregation reads the issue AND
+its linked PRs.
+
+```json
+{"v":1,"agent":"han","envelope_id":"…","stage_label":"ready-for-implementation",
+ "issue":"matty-v/snapdex#42","window":{"from":"<iso8601>","to":"<iso8601>"},
+ "models":{"claude-sonnet-4-5":{"input":812345,"output":41210,"cache_read":9130221,"cache_creation":420110,"api_calls":63}},
+ "charter_variant":"full@9c63b54","quality":"exact","reason":null}
+```
+
+**Truthfulness ladder (NORMATIVE — extends the no-fabrication directive, Matt 2026-06-07):**
+`quality` is `exact` (intact transcript tree), `lower_bound` (files rotated/compacted mid-stage
+were EXCLUDED — the figure is a floor, `reason` says why), or `unavailable` (no baseline / nothing
+measurable — `models` is empty). Consumers render `unavailable` as
+`token usage: unavailable (<reason>)` and `lower_bound` with a `≥` prefix. **Never 0, never a
+guess, never a hand-edited marker.**
+
+### 10.3 `falcon:charter:v1` — Lando, appended to the ISSUE BODY at kickoff
+
+The mini-charter: scope + planned crew (from `config/team-roster.yaml`) + active charter variant.
+Same idiom as the `<!-- discord-thread: <id> -->` marker. Human twin: the 🧭 Team-plan card in
+the issue's Discord thread.
+
+```json
+{"v":1,"issue":"matty-v/snapdex#42","kickoff_at":"<iso8601>",
+ "planned":[{"agent":"yoda","role":"product-triage","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5"}],
+ "charter_variant":"full@9c63b54"}
+```
+
+### 10.4 Close-path aggregation (Lando, process-worker-ack Step 6b)
+
+At issue close Lando: collects every `falcon:usage:v1` on the issue + linked PRs (duplicate
+envelope_ids are ALL kept — re-dispatch is real kickback spend); prices per model from
+`config/provider-rates.yaml` (suffix-normalized lookup; a model with no rate renders **unpriced**
+and the total is flagged partial — never $0.00; `rates_provenance` from `.meta` travels with every
+total); cross-checks Kyber's windowed metrics API and LABELS any discrepancy (e.g. "platform
+metric excludes output tokens") instead of averaging it away; posts the completion-summary cost
+lines; appends one JSON line to `lando-agent/reports/cost-ledger.jsonl` (committed with the ship
+report). Any `unavailable` stage forces `totals.priced:false`, `cost_usd:null`, and an honest
+"cost: partial" card. The ledger row shape is documented in `lando-agent/skills/
+process-worker-ack.md` Step 6b.
+
